"url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"A new page needs three things or it will not appear in the sidebar and the coverage gate\nfails: the file under `docs/`, an entry in the nav (see above), and a listing in\n`_HAND_WRITTEN_MD` in `docs/BUILD.bazel` so Bazel ships it as a runfile."},"209":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-32","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#information-architecture","content":"Use the right-hand ToC for long pages. Keep navigation focused."},"210":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-33","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Every page must open (after the title or any intentional top widget such as the interactive panel) with a scannable overview in this bullet-point format:\n**What's on this page**"},"211":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-34","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Bullets describing the main content, sections, diagrams, tables, etc.\n**What this enables / practical use**"},"212":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-35","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Bullets describing reader benefit, common use cases, or what the content lets you achieve.\nWrite those labels as bold markdown plus lists, not as JSX. The site wraps the first pair into a two-column panel; later examples on the same page stay ordinary prose."},"213":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-36","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Write for humans. Be concise. Remove filler."},"214":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-37","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Include copy-pasteable examples."},"215":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-38","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Use Mermaid for diagrams (supported)."},"216":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-39","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Prefer `<Callout type=\"info|warning|error\" title=\"…\">` for asides and `<Tabs>`/`<Tab>` for\nalternatives. The `!!!` and `=== \"Title\"` syntax is **not** parsed any more — the migration\nrewrote existing uses, and new content uses the components directly (see\n`docs-site/components/mdx-components.tsx` for what is importable)."},"217":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-40","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Pages that need those components are `.mdx`; pages that do not can stay `.md`. Both are\nvalid MDX, so plain Markdown keeps working unchanged."},"218":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-41","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Escape what MDX would otherwise read as JSX: a literal `<` in prose or code needs `&lt;`,\nand `{`/`}` outside a code fence must be `&#123;`/`&#125;`."},"219":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-42","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"Always link to source code or exact commands when possible."},"220":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-43","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#content-guidelines","content":"**Human review required**: All AI-assisted drafts must be reviewed and edited by a human before merging."},"221":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-44","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#code-generated-command-reference-shell","content":"The Shell Commands & Helpers page is **not** written by hand. It is produced from structured comments inside the scripts."},"222":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-45","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#code-generated-command-reference-shell","content":"**Markers you must use** (these are what the generator looks for):"},"223":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-46","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#code-generated-command-reference-shell","content":"**Full workflow**"},"224":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-47","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#code-generated-command-reference-shell","content":"Edit `scripts/manage.sh` or `scripts/lib/*.sh`."},"225":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-48","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#code-generated-command-reference-shell","content":"Add or improve a `# ##` / `# @command` block with rich, accurate docs (over-document — the user asked for this)."},"226":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-49","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#code-generated-command-reference-shell","content":"`bazelisk run //docs:docs` (or serve)."},"227":{"id":"/CONTRIBUTING-50","page_id":"/CONTRIBUTING","tags":["documentation","contributing","fumadocs","nextjs","bazel"],"type":"text","url":"/CONTRIBUTING#code-gene